Reliaburger diagnosis: test (2 nodes)
collected at unix 10

crashloops: critical
  CRITICAL [crashloop] app api/default restarted repeatedly (app.api/default)
    instance api-0 restarted 3 times in the last 15 minutes
    related restart at 9: exit code 1
    next: app api is crashlooping; inspect its recent logs and run `relish rollback api` if this started after a deploy
  tests: Counts each instance's `restart` events in every node's event ring (the
         same ones `relish events` shows) inside a recent window. Enough of them
         for one instance is critical, with any recent deploy and the app's
         first error log line attached. Replicas that restarted once each are
         not a crash loop, and a lifetime restart count is not an input.
  threshold: 3 (CRASHLOOP_RESTARTS): restarts of one instance inside the window that make a crash loop
  threshold: 15 minutes (CRASHLOOP_WINDOW_SECONDS): the window restarts are counted in
  threshold: 30 minutes (RECENT_DEPLOY_SECONDS): a deploy started this recently is named as the likely cause
  docs: https://github.com/reliaburger/reliaburger/blob/main/docs/manual/07_diagnostics.md#relish-wtf-whats-broken-and-why
  manual: relish manual diagnostics

disks: warning
  WARNING [disk-high] node node-1 filesystem for images is 88.0% full (node.node-1)
    next: node node-1 disk is at 88.0%; list images with `relish images`, delete tags you no longer need with `relish images delete <repository:tag>` (untagged images expire after [images] gc_retain_days), or lower log and metric retention in node.toml
  WARNING [disk-high] node node-2 filesystem for images is 90.5% full (node.node-2)
    next: node node-2 disk is at 90.5%; list images with `relish images`, delete tags you no longer need with `relish images delete <repository:tag>` (untagged images expire after [images] gc_retain_days), or lower log and metric retention in node.toml
  tests: Reads how full each node's filesystem is for every storage domain it
         holds (data, images, logs, metrics, volumes), from the node's
         diagnostics.
  threshold: 85% (DISK_WARNING_PERCENT): used space that makes it a warning
  threshold: 95% (DISK_CRITICAL_PERCENT): used space that makes it critical
  docs: https://github.com/reliaburger/reliaburger/blob/main/docs/manual/12_operations.md#sizing-a-nodes-disk
  manual: relish manual operations

alerts: unknown
  UNKNOWN [alerts] cluster: node node-2: alerts: timed out after 5s
  tests: Reads the Mayo alert rules every node evaluates. Each firing alert is a
         warning.
  docs: https://github.com/reliaburger/reliaburger/blob/main/docs/manual/04_observability.md#alerts
  manual: relish manual observability

nodes: ok
  OK: all 2 nodes alive
  tests: Reads the cluster's member list and asks every member's Bun API for its
         health through the node you're connected to. A member that doesn't
         answer is critical, and so is one that Mustard gossip marks dead or
         suspect.
  docs: https://github.com/reliaburger/reliaburger/blob/main/docs/manual/02_cluster-basics.md#watch-it
  manual: relish manual cluster-basics

council: ok
  OK: council quorum healthy (2/2)
  tests: Reads the council membership and every node's own view of it. No
         leader, fewer members answering than a majority (members / 2 + 1), two
         leaders, two recovery epochs or a fenced node is critical; a missing
         member while quorum holds, a voter applying the log more slowly than
         the others, or a retired-identity list 90% full, is a warning. A
         standalone node needs no council and is OK.
  threshold: 100 (VOTER_LAG_WARNING): applied log entries behind the furthest voter
  threshold: 90% (RETIRED_IDENTITY_WARNING_PERCENT): of the 65,536 retired identities a cluster can hold
  docs: https://github.com/reliaburger/reliaburger/blob/main/docs/manual/12_operations.md#a-walk-through-a-recovery
  manual: relish manual operations

Summary: 1 critical, 2 warning, 1 unknown, 2 OK
